
  [1mA. Mutable task rows + append-only event log.[0m [38;5;153mtasks[39m holds current state; every mutation also appends to [38;5;153mtask_events[39m
  ([38;5;153mtask_id[39m, [38;5;153mactor_id[39m, [38;5;153mtype[39m, [38;5;153mpayload[39m, [38;5;153mcreated_at[39m) inside the same transaction. Events are [3msemantic[0m — [38;5;153mtask.assigned[39m,
  [38;5;153mtask.status_changed[39m, [38;5;153mtask.commented[39m — not raw field diffs, so a notification can say "Dana assigned you [3mFix login[0m"
  rather than "a field changed". Reads stay ordinary SQL. The risk is drift: a write that bypasses the service layer
  records no event. Mitigated by funnelling every mutation through one [38;5;153mtaskService[39m module, which is also the natural
  place subscriptions hook in later. [3mComplexity: moderate.[0m

  [1mB. Full event sourcing.[0m Events are the only source of truth; task state is a projection rebuilt from them. Drift
  becomes structurally impossible and history is perfect. But it brings replay, projection rebuilds, and event-schema
  versioning — and every read becomes a question about the projection's freshness. That's a lot of machinery to protect
  a task list. [3mComplexity: high.[0m

  [1mC. Derive events from row diffs[0m (SQLite triggers or [38;5;153mupdated_at[39m polling). No application discipline needed; catches
  writes from anywhere, including manual ones. But triggers don't know who the actor is — SQLite has no session context
  — so you'd have to smuggle the user in anyway, and the events come out as field diffs rather than meaning. That
  reintroduces the vague-notification problem we chose this path to avoid. [3mComplexity: trivial to build, expensive to [0m
  [3mlive with.[0m

  I recommend [1mA[0m. It gets the property that actually matters — durable, attributed, semantic events written
  transactionally with the change — without event sourcing's overhead, and the single-service-layer constraint it
  requires is something a small app should have regardless.
